# Trivy CVE allowlist for Spring Petclinic Microservices
#
# Format: one CVE-ID per line with an optional comment.
# Entries here are skipped during Trivy scans in CI (build-push.yml).
#
# Before adding a CVE to this file:
#   1. Confirm the CVE is a false positive or has an accepted risk.
#   2. Add a comment explaining why it is accepted and when to revisit.
#   3. Review this file quarterly and remove entries for patched CVEs.
#
# Example:
# CVE-2023-XXXXX  # false positive: affects feature not used in this project; revisit 2026-Q3
